<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan Sept M2 money supply up 8.69 percent yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Taiwan Sept M2 money supply up 8.69 percent yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's broadest money supply measure, M2, grew 8.69 percent in September compared with September 1995, the central bank said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Like the year-on-year rise of 8.44 percent in August, the September rise failed to reach the central bank's 9-14 percent M2 growth target.</p>
<p>				September 1996     August 1996</p>
<p> M2 ANNUAL RATE		 +8.69		+8.44</p>
<p> M1B ANNUAL RATE		+4.67		+4.38</p>
<p> M1A ANNUAL RATE		+1.42		+1.49</p>
<p>Note - M1A is cash, checking accounts and passbook deposits. M1B is M1A plus savings accounts. M2 is M1B plus quasi-money.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
